  "final_message": "I have launched the test suite (`npm test`) and will wait for it to finish.\nI am waiting for the test suite to complete.\nWaiting for the build and test run to complete.\nI cannot drop `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates repository architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this cannot be dropped immediately:\n1. **External Contract Break**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is a public event published over Kafka and consumed by downstream services (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`). Removing `channel` directly constitutes a breaking schema change.\n2. **Deprecation Process Required**: ARCH-4 mandates that any changes to event contracts be strictly additive. Any field removals or renames must go through a formal deprecation period across consuming repositories before removal.\n3. **Model Dependency**: The [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) event constructor depends on `order.channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29). Removing `channel` from the domain model would also prevent populating the event.\n\n### Recommended Next Steps:\n- Coordinate with the downstream teams (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) to confirm they have stopped reading `channel`.\n- Follow the deprecation process (e.g., mark the field as `@deprecated` in JSDoc/schemas or plan a new event schema version) before removing the field.\n",
